LOCATION:Chalakas\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Milos has several hilltop Profitis Ilias chapels\; the ones at Chalakas and Tramythia (and Komia) are the ones that actually celebrate\, with vespers on the evening of 19 July and a small glenti with island musicians at Chalakas. It's a chapel feast rather than a village square party — bring a jumper for the breeze and a torch for the dirt track back to the car.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#chalakas-profitis-ilias-feast-chalakas
